# tutor: the whole of `merl --tutor`, each lesson's answer as the tutor's tests press it, to the
# three review lessons at its end (#158): the sample project becomes an agent's uncommitted work
# over one commit, the review panel takes the left, `c` walks cli.py on into models.py, `C` walks
# back, and `m` ticks store.py. Each lesson opens as a card in the middle, the code dimmed behind
# it, and Enter sends it into the box at the bottom before the answer; on lesson 9, `i` brings the
# card back (#501)
merl --tutor
wait Enter starts
key Enter o
type store
key Enter
wait Tutor 2/
key Enter /
type load_config
key Enter Enter n Enter d Enter [ Enter ] Enter u
wait Usages
key Down Enter Enter s
type TODO
wait reject a note
key Enter
wait Tutor 9/
key Enter i
wait Enter starts
key Enter D
type NoteStore
wait store.py:9
key Enter
wait Tutor 10/
key Enter :
type 42
key Enter Enter } Enter { Enter v v v Enter t Enter Tab Enter Enter Enter Enter
type #hi
key Escape Enter C-z Enter w Enter p Enter f Enter Escape
wait Tutor 23/
key Enter Escape
wait Tutor 24/
key Enter c*6
wait Tutor 25/
key Enter C
wait Tutor 26/
key Enter m
wait That is all of merl
